# @PKG_NAME@

ONNX Runtime @ORT_VERSION@ with the MIGraphX GPU execution provider, for
AMD GPUs (@GPU_TARGETS@) on ROCm @ROCM_VERSION@ (TheRock amdrocm packages).
Installed by this package; see the `description` field of the .deb for
details.

## Using it from darktable

darktable keeps its bundled CPU ONNX Runtime and only switches to this GPU
stack via a library path override:

    # darktaberc
    plugins/ai/ort_library_path = /usr/lib/@PKG_NAME@/lib/libonnxruntime.so.@ORT_VERSION@

    # or environment
    export DT_ORT_LIBRARY=/usr/lib/@PKG_NAME@/lib/libonnxruntime.so.@ORT_VERSION@

## Verifying the installation

    /usr/lib/@PKG_NAME@/test/test_darktable_path /usr/lib/@PKG_NAME@/lib/libonnxruntime.so.@ORT_VERSION@
    cd /usr/lib/@PKG_NAME@/test && ./test_ort_mgx test_mgx.onnx x_input.bin y_expected.bin 4

Notes:

- The first inference run of each model is slow (MIGraphX Triton JIT for
  @GPU_TARGETS@); compiled results are cached under ~/.cache/migraphx.
- The ROCm runtime is **not** part of this package — it is provided by the
  amdrocm packages listed in `Depends`.

## Uninstalling

    sudo apt-get purge @PKG_NAME@

(purging also removes the ld.so.conf.d fragment that postinst may have
created.)
